## Architecture A - integration response template for every mapped error (400, 404)
##
## A Lambda that fails reports this payload to API Gateway:
##
##   { "errorMessage": "...", "errorType": "...", "stackTrace": [ ... ] }
##
## com.eci.orders.adapter.lambda.custom.ApiError makes errorMessage *be* the JSON error body of
## the API, so this template only has to copy it out. Writing the string unquoted is what keeps it
## a JSON object instead of a JSON string.
##
##   errorMessage = {"error":"ORDER_NOT_FOUND","message":"Order ORD-999 does not exist"}
##   response     = {"error":"ORDER_NOT_FOUND","message":"Order ORD-999 does not exist"}
##
## The status code itself is not decided here: it comes from the integration response whose
## selection pattern matched the error code (see infra/openapi-custom.yaml).
$input.path('$.errorMessage')
